D. entries the run reports as p == 0: 1
      LIG1_REC1      CTA|CTB    reported p = 0.0 ;  exact documented p = 0.0006 ;  floor 1/1680 = 0.000595

   The documented 'equal or higher' rule cannot return 0 -- the observed labelling is
   itself one of the 1680 assignments and ties with itself -- and the standard
   permutation correction (b+1)/(m+1) has a floor of 1/(iterations+1). Downstream
   plotting turns p = 0 into -log10(p) = inf.

E. footnote on arithmetic: cluster means are float32 (counts are cast to float32 by
   counts_preprocessor, and numpy_groupies returns float32), so permutations that are
   mathematically tied with the observed value can land on either side of the strict
   comparison by ~1e-7 of rounding noise.
   tie mass counted in exact arithmetic (float64): median 0.0458, max 0.2024
   tie mass seen by the shipped float32 comparison: median 0.0345, max 0.2024
   -> part of the tied mass is already split arbitrarily by rounding before the
      strict-vs-inclusive question is even reached.
